<title>SOUTH KOREA: S.Korea's Jan-Apr oil products demand edges lower.</title>
<headline>S.Korea's Jan-Apr oil products demand edges lower.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's petroleum product demand slipped to 263.3 million barrels in the first four months of 1997 from 264.2 million a year earlier, the Ministry of Trade, Industry and Energy said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The fall in demand was due mainly to an industrial slowdown, energy conservation campaign and increasing use of liquefied natural gas at homes, a ministry statement said.</p>
<p>Despite the slowdown in demand, South Korea's oil products output rose sharply to 299.4 million barrels in the first four months from 232.2 million a year ago.  </p>
<p>Oil products demand (in million barrels)</p>
<p>				    Jan-Apr	 Jan-Apr 1996</p>
<p>    TOTAL			  263.3	    264.2</p>
<p>MAJOR PRODUCTS</p>
<p>     gasoline		     21.4	     21.2</p>
<p>     kerosene		     35.8	     34.7</p>
<p>     diesel			 59.5	     65.7</p>
<p>     C-type fuel oil	    60.0	     58.1</p>
<p>     naphtha			50.4	     48.8</p>
<p>     LPG			    25.8	     26.0</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5643</p>
